Well now it seems long back but I know it is not as old as I might feel. I spend almost a year in the famous city Kota which is located in the state of rajasthan. The city said to be where the greatest minds needs to pass through, atleast that's what I was told. 

Just a quick disclaimer here, when I say city, it doesn't mean the local people, culture, language etc. It is a beautiful city, kind people and a nice place. What i refer to is the prevalent idea of what this city is, or it is most talked to in that context.

The first experience when you step out on a train station, probably before than that, you'll encounter it. The relentless bombardment of your field of view with their advertisemnt. Does not matter where you look, it was everywhere. Those big hoarding with young men with AIR 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9..... seemed like gods. They were really, they seemed big, eternal and inreachable. What you some small creature can expect to be atleast be part of that race, and just get somewhere. Where, we don't know.
Who know, maybe other people definitely would right? Maybe I am the most lost of all of them. The more I talked, the more i realised that these ones are more confused than me because atleas t I know I am confused. It will be injustice to say that I have more clarity now than earlier but atleast.